{"ts":"2026-07-11T02:58:27.882Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-xspd"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Close the jscpd/CodeFactor sensitivity gap: minTokens 115 misses low-token table clones the CodeFactor bot still files"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Evidence 2026-07-11: pnpm lint:duplicates on main reports 0 clones (562 files, minLines 22 / minTokens 115) while CodeFactor filed GH-508 for a 28-line byte-identical object-literal table duplicated between create.ts:335-362 and update.ts:260-287. Short-identifier object rows stay under 115 tokens across 28 lines, so the zero-duplication gate from PR#506/pm-7wmq is structurally blind to table-shaped clones that CodeFactor's thresholds catch. Fixing pm-zuw8 clears this instance but not the class; result is recurring CodeFactor auto-issues despite a green local gate. Successor to closed parity item pm-6sqo."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Chore"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["codefactor","duplication","quality-gate"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-11T02:58:27.882Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-11T02:58:27.882Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"jscpd config detects the GH-508-class clone shape (create.ts/update.ts normalizer tables) on a pre-fix checkout, via lowered minTokens or a second low-token/high-line profile; lint:duplicates still passes on main after pm-zuw8 lands; false-positive review documented if thresholds are lowered"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-92if"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-zuw8","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-11T02:58:27.882Z"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":".jscpd.json","scope":"project"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"3c85e36ddd3940178213f6e4a0383bd6271365dde236f9c2ec7e0e96a2e26ab2","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-07-25T07:14:41.244Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T07:14:41.244Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-25T07:14:41.243Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Sensitivity measurement 2026-07-25 quantifying the blind spot. At the committed .jscpd.json thresholds (minLines 22, minTokens 115, strict mode, 748 files / 418,637 lines) the repo reports zero clones — a clean pass. Re-running the identical file set at minLines 12 / minTokens 60 reports 402 clone groups, 6,403 duplicated lines (1.53%) and 34,408 duplicated tokens, so the entire duplication signal lives between the two settings. Composition of the lower-threshold set: the large majority are test files (static-quality-gate.spec.ts, sentry-telemetry-gate.spec.ts, sdk/graph/*.spec.ts, sdk/merge-safety.spec.ts, workspace-transaction.spec.ts, smoke-*.spec.ts), which is the pm-ld0z spec-decomposition territory rather than product duplication. Product-side groups worth triage: src/cli/commands/copy.ts around lines 118-136 appears in ten overlapping groups against multiple partners, src/cli/commands/create.ts at 338 and 1025, src/cli/error-guidance.ts at 452 and 508, src/cli/commands/reindex.ts at 894 and 1133, src/cli/main.ts at 3285, src/cli/register-mutation.ts at 54-90, plus per-package clones in packages/pm-beads, pm-calendar, pm-governance-audit, pm-guide-shell, pm-linked-test-adapters and pm-templates runtimes. The copy.ts cluster is the strongest single candidate: one region matching ten partners is the signature of a table or option-mapping shape that wants a shared helper."}]}],"before_hash":"3c85e36ddd3940178213f6e4a0383bd6271365dde236f9c2ec7e0e96a2e26ab2","after_hash":"e0f90df03919352ce011f63b6f9f65fd73910db1145d59871b88fdf37016a41e"}
{"ts":"2026-07-25T21:39:12.318Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-25T21:39:12.318Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Cross-file duplication census 2026-07-25, run against the shipped tree with jscpd strict mode at 12 lines / 60 tokens over src, packages and scripts. The repository gate (22 lines / 115 tokens) reports zero clones on the same tree, so everything below is invisible to it — this is the sensitivity gap this item owns, measured rather than argued.\n\n112 clone pairs total, 47 of them cross-file. The cross-file set is not noise; it partitions into four coherent classes:\n\n1. History maintenance pipeline (7 pairs) — redact/repair/compact/read plus cli copy and restore. Filed as pm-34w8za; that item carries the pair list.\n2. CLI re-implementing SDK logic (4 pairs) — cli/commands/comments.ts:100 vs sdk/annotations.ts:219, cli/commands/calendar.ts:1019 vs sdk/query/list.ts:1000, cli/commands/update-many.ts:704 vs pm-governance-audit/normalize.ts:227, cli/register-mutation.ts:54 vs sdk/cli-contracts/tool-schema.ts:600 (37 lines, the largest pair in the repository). This class is the SDK-first inversion pm-usfg tracks; duplication detection is how it shows up mechanically.\n3. Package activation boilerplate (5 pairs) — pm-beads vs pm-todos runtime.ts three times, pm-guide-shell vs pm-linked-test-adapters, pm-calendar vs pm-governance-audit vs pm-search-advanced flag tables. Every first-party package hand-rolls the same loader and the same standard filter-flag declarations; nothing in the SDK offers them.\n4. Contract table restatements (3 pairs) — core/store/settings-validator.ts:37 vs types.ts:1175, core/extensions/extension-types.ts:200 vs sdk/extension.ts:459, sdk/files.ts:39 vs sdk/linked-artifacts.ts:69.\n\nClass 4 is the shape that produced GH-508 in the first place. Classes 2 and 3 are the ones a threshold change would newly surface, and both are pointing at real missing abstractions rather than at cosmetic copying, so lowering the threshold is likely to be productive rather than merely noisy. Suggested calibration evidence when this item is worked: 12/60 yields 47 cross-file pairs with a 0.94 percent duplicated-token rate over 823k tokens, which is a workable starting gate if the four classes above are cleared first."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T21:39:12.318Z"}],"before_hash":"e0f90df03919352ce011f63b6f9f65fd73910db1145d59871b88fdf37016a41e","after_hash":"f939a71423cbbc35e88d7bdb5cd9347fb5bb6382cc6e9cc8718a0a1d7d5b8d79"}
